ning from its encounters with scenery and objects through trial-and-error. Once these behaviours are learn, the PiT will know how to respond to those objects in the future (such as a Flower, or a Spike). Whenever the PiT becomes injured, or tired, returning it to its home will allow Dr. Y to fix it. The objective then becomes for your PiT to solve puzzles on its own - for which it will be rewarded with AI upgrade chips.", "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/pet-in-tv", "videos": [{"id": 150153, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "CsE7NYbUMFI", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CsE7NYbUMFI", "title": "\u304c\u3093\u3070\u308c\u68ee\u5ddd\u541b2\u53f7 #1", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CsE7NYbUMFI/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}